        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF147 Relnote: CSS Module scripts]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42306</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42306"/>
        <updated>2025-12-09T02:36:08.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF147 adds support for module scripts in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1986681" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1986681</a>. This allows you to do stuff like below to import a stylesheet and adopt it into your document.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="import sheet from './styles.css' with { type: 'css' };
document.adoptedStyleSheets = [sheet];"><pre class="notranslate"><span class="pl-k">import</span> <span class="pl-s1">sheet</span> <span class="pl-k">from</span> <span class="pl-s">'./styles.css'</span> <span class="pl-k">with</span> <span class="pl-kos">{</span> <span class="pl-c1">type</span>: <span class="pl-s">'css'</span> <span class="pl-kos">}</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-smi">document</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-c1">adoptedStyleSheets</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-kos">[</span><span class="pl-s1">sheet</span><span class="pl-kos">]</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">This adds a release note.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3699248949" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42255" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/42255/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42255">#42255</a></p>]]></content>
